-- lib/polyproc.cub — interface-reshaping guarded processes (PolyTr / OrgTr over clocked GProc).
--
-- lib/proc.cub defines GProc κ S A over a static command signature S : Sig: every continuation
-- remains in the same signature S for the entire lifetime of the process. As docs/to-david-spivak.cub
-- notes (referencing Spivak's February 2026 PolyTr / OrgTr), learning, chemical reactions,
-- conformational protein gating, cell differentiation, and Michael Levin's movable self-boundaries
-- (gap-junction coupling vs cancer decoupling) all require interactions that reshape the interface
-- itself.
--
-- Constructed and checked here:
--   1. DynSig: an indexed signature (positions I, commands/responses S i, and interface transition
--      ds-next specifying how each (command, response) reshapes the interface for the next tick).
--   2. RProc κ D A i: clocked guarded processes indexed by interface state i : ds-idx D, where
--      each command/response pair (c, r) moves the continuation to interface state (ds-next D i c r).
--   3. Faithful embedding of static GProc into RProc over const-ds (gproc-to-rproc, rproc-to-gproc,
--      and exact guarded round-trip paths gproc-rproc-id, rproc-gproc-id).
--   4. GatedDS: a concrete dynamic-boundary signature (two-mode interface: coupled / decoupled,
--      or open / closed ion-channel gate) where an interaction flips the interface mid-run.
import "core.hypercubical"
import "proc.hypercubical"

